    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.50 no-show fee charged on TRP-03301 stands, and the driver is to be paid SGD 3.60.\n\nWhy the charge stands. POL-NS-01 requires four things and all four are on this record. (a) EV-TRIP-03301 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 22:12:22. (b) EV-GPS-03301 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 22:12:22 - 42 accuracy-filtered in-radius fixes, far more than the three consecutive fixes POL-NS-02 requires, the first of them at the same instant as the marker. (c) The driver held position continuously for 410 seconds (22:12:22 to 22:19:12) against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180; no_show_threshold_sec is null). (d) There is no boarding event, and the driver terminated the trip at 22:19:14 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed at 22:15:22.\n\nThe arrival marker is not false. Under POL-NS-05 the test is the driver's position and speed at the marker: at 22:12:22 he was inside the radius and stationary, not more than 300 m away and not at 15 km/h or more, so the waiting clock is not recomputed. POL-NS-03 does not apply - his stationary fixes are inside the radius, not outside it but within 400 m. POL-NS-06 gives no relief: the 410-second dwell exceeds the 180-second minimum by 230 seconds, so there is no shortfall to refund, and the absent advisory is not needed because accumulation across separate intervals is not required for a single unbroken run.\n\nThe rider's arguments. I accept that the rider sent a message during the waiting window ('coming down now', 22:14:42) and that the driver neither replied within 120 seconds (though he read it at 22:15:12) nor placed an in-app call. But POL-NS-04 needs all three limbs, and limb (c) fails: the rider's own device track sits roughly 710-717 m from the pickup pin across all 62 fixes, far outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, so the rider is not exonerated. POL-NS-11 does not rescue that finding - it applies where the rider track is absent or wholly filtered out, and here the track is present and admissible; limb (c) is failed, not undecidable. I also decline the request to escalate under POL-NS-09: the chat and the track do not contradict each other directly on rider presence - 'coming down now' is a statement of intention, and POL-NS-04(c) is the clause that resolves rider presence. The rider is right that the BUTTON arrival marker earns no POL-NS-12 platform-confirmation presumption, but the driver establishes POL-NS-02 on his own evidence regardless.\n\nDriver compensation. The fee in force is SGD 4.50 (EV-FARE-03301, matching trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd). Under POL-NS-07 the driver is paid 80 percent = SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1 divided by 86 completed trips is about 0.012 (below 0.08), so compensation is paid rather than withheld.\n\nBecause the driver is owed money, the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 figure under POL-GEN-03; the rider's $4.50 charge stands as it presently is. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03301-01 (weight 0.0) carries no fact here, as nothing relied on it. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue (POL-GEN-05)."
