seconds with no in-app call (limb (b)), limb (c) is not met: your own device track (EV-GPS-03301) records your device stationary roughly 710 m from the pin throughout, with no fix inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius (rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0), so the rider was not at the pickup. If the track were instead treated as unrunnable, POL-NS-11 makes limb (c) undecidable rather than failed, and the clause still cannot exonerate you — the fee is decided on the driver's own evidence. Either way POL-NS-04 does not apply. Your POL-NS-09 escalation argument also fails: the supposed conflict between your 'coming down now' message and your device's position goes to whether the rider was at the pickup, which is not the fact that decides this fee — the driver's arrival and dwell are, and those are consistent across the trip record and the trace. POL-NS-04(c), read with POL-NS-11, is the clause that governs rider presence, so POL-NS-09(b)'s 'no clause resolves the conflict' condition is not satisfied, and no other POL-NS-09 trigger (confidence, repeat-party disputes, anti-farming, sole impaired evidence) is present. You are right that arrival rests on a driver-pressed BUTTON marker, so POL-NS-12's platform-confirmation shortcut does not apply; I give the marker no presumption — and none is needed, because POL-NS-02's own test is met.\n\nThe money. Because POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force = SGD 3.60 (the net figure, not the SGD 6.61 gross). The anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (below 4) and 1/86 ≈ 0.012 (below 0.08), so compensation is paid rather than withheld. Under POL-GEN-03 this is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling, in which amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 the ruling moves and the rider's SGD 4.50 charge stands. No clause produces a referral. Confidence is 0.9: the deciding facts are carried by EV-TR